# -- go2cs specific exclusions --

# Roslyn source-generator output (EmitCompilerGeneratedFiles writes these to
# each project's Generated/ folder). They are regenerated on every build and
# must not be tracked.
*.g.cs

# Don't ignore the debug folder in src/core
!src/core/debug/
!src/core/debug/*

# But do ignore any debug/bin/obj folders in subdirectories
src/core/debug/**/[Dd]ebug/
src/core/debug/**/[Bb]in/
src/core/debug/**/[Oo]bj/

# Don't ignore the debug folder in src/core/runtime
!src/core/runtime/debug/
!src/core/runtime/debug/*

# But do ignore any debug/bin/obj folders in subdirectories
src/core/runtime/debug/**/[Dd]ebug/
src/core/runtime/debug/**/[Bb]in/
src/core/runtime/debug/**/[Oo]bj/


# Don't ignore the log folder in src/core
!src/core/log/
!src/core/log/*

# But do ignore any debug/bin/obj folders in subdirectories
src/core/log/**/[Dd]ebug/
src/core/log/**/[Bb]in/
src/core/log/**/[Oo]bj/

/src/go2cs/go2cs.exe
/src/go2cs/go2cs

# Per-run reports a `-stdlib` conversion writes at its output root. Since the converted stdlib
# moved home to src/core, a regen "in place" (-go2cspath <repo>/src) drops these into src/ —
# they are regenerable run output, not source. go2cs.slnx lists them as <File> entries so they
# are browsable when present.
/src/graphs/
/src/reports/
/src/stdlib_conversion_progress.txt

# GitHub Copilot custom instructions file (may be auto-created by Visual Studio)
.github/copilot-instructions.md
src/.github/copilot-instructions.md

# AI/working scratch (build logs, reconvert overlays) — never commit
scratchpad/

# A converted package's testdata is SOURCE — the fixture corpus its Go test suite reads — and a
# banked row promises it reproduces from a clone. But the "Files built by Visual Studio" block
# above matches by EXTENSION across the whole tree, and Go names fixtures for what they contain,
# not for how they were built: `debug/elf`'s twenty DWARF-relocation objects are `*.obj`, so
# `*.obj` silently swallowed every one of them at banking time (found 2026-08-19 — `debug/elf` is
# the first banked package whose testdata collides with a build-output pattern; `debug/dwarf`'s
# equivalents are `.elf`/`.elf4` and were never touched). Last matching pattern wins, so this
# un-ignores the corpus testdata trees wholesale rather than chasing one extension at a time —
# the same whole-tree scope `.gitattributes` already gives them with `src/core/**/testdata/** -text`.
# `src/core/.gitignore`'s `*.go` rule still applies: a deeper .gitignore takes precedence, so
# staged Go source copies stay ignored.
!src/core/**/testdata/**

# Session worktrees. These are ignored on the coordinator box only through .git/info/exclude, which
# is LOCAL and never committed — so on any other machine `git add .claude/...` would sweep hundreds
# of thousands of worktree files into a commit. Committing `.claude/rules/` and `.claude/skills/`
# (the CLAUDE.md split, 2026-09-12, docs/PLAN-context-diet.md) is what puts tracked content under
# `.claude/` for the first time and makes that reachable, so the rule is tracked here rather than
# left to each clone's private exclude file.
**/.claude/worktrees/
